# OperatorBench — line-ending and diff policy
#
# THE RULE THAT MATTERS MOST: frozen artifacts are stored BYTE-EXACT.
#
# data/ and results/ files were written by Windows Python and contain CRLF. Their
# sha256 hashes are recorded in data/**/manifest*.json, results/environment.json
# and results/f10_f11_frozen.json, and are re-checked by
# scripts/capture_environment.py. If git normalised their line endings, every one
# of those hashes would mismatch after a fresh clone — D-09's frozen-dataset
# guarantee would be broken silently, and the paper's reproducibility claim with
# it. Verified: abstracts_v1.csv is 4e273eae5ac4ec16 as CRLF and d616788a93471c64
# as LF.
#
# So: -text on everything frozen. No conversion, in or out, ever.
data/**    -text
results/** -text
logs_manifest.json -text

# Normalize ordinary source and prose. Frozen protocol sources are excepted below.
# This repo is worked on
# from a Windows venv and a Linux shell against the same directory; without a
# policy, core.autocrlf rewrites files on checkout and every one looks modified
# from the other side, burying real diffs.
*.py   text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
*.txt  text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
*.cfg  text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.tex  text eol=lf
*.bib  text eol=lf
.gitignore     text eol=lf
.gitattributes text eol=lf

# These exact source bytes are bound by completed experiment manifests.
scripts/prepare_revision_evaluation.py -text
scripts/run_revision_evaluation.py -text
scripts/run_matched_control.py -text
harness/admission.py -text
harness/revision.py -text
harness/revision_assertions.py -text
harness/intercept.py -text
docs/REVISION-EVALUATION.md -text
artifacts/revision-evaluation-20261008/** -text
audits/** -text

# Binary — never diff or merge.
*.png  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.xlsx binary
*.pptx binary
*.docx binary
*.zip  binary
*.db   binary

# Large frozen inputs: keep them out of `git diff` noise. They are verified by
# sha256 in their manifests, not by reading diffs.
data/abstracts/abstracts_v1.csv -diff
data/reviews/reviews_v1.csv     -diff
